---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, index, url } from "../lib/data";
const jsonld = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite", name: site.title, url: new URL(url("/"), Astro.site).href, inLanguage: "en" };
---
<Base title={site.title} jsonld={jsonld}>
  <h1>{site.title}</h1>
  <p class="lede">English translations of Chinese Buddhist texts that have no translation from an approved source. Each line is read through the lectures of an approved teacher, and the page shows why it reads the way it does.</p>
  <div class="notice">
    <p><strong>AI translations, following an approved teacher's lectures.</strong> The English is made by AI under human direction, choosing between the readings the Chinese allows as the teacher reads them, then checked line by line by a second AI review against the Chinese and the teacher's own words; the project owner reviews what that check flags. Not an official translation. <a href={url("method/")}>Read the method and its measured error rate</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Texts</h2>
  {index.texts.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">The first translation is under review. It appears here once every line has been checked.</p>
  ) : (
    <ul class="cards">
      {index.texts.map((t) => (
        <li><a class="card" href={url(`${t.slug}/`)}>
          <h3>{t.title_en}</h3>
          <p class="zh" lang="zh-Hant">{t.title_zh}</p>
          <p>{t.author_en} · CBETA {t.id} · {t.n_segs} lines · read with {t.teacher_en}</p>
          <p style="margin-top:8px">{t.certified
            ? <span class="pill accent">AI-checked{t.n_owner > 0 ? ` · ${t.n_owner} lines owner-reviewed` : ""}</span>
            : <span class="pill warn">draft: {t.n_certified}/{t.n_segs} lines checked</span>}</p>
        </a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  )}
  <h2 class="section-title">Related</h2>
  <p>The teachers' lectures these readings come from, as Chinese study notes and full transcripts: <a href={`${site.notes}/`} lang="zh-Hant">講經筆記</a>.</p>
</Base>
